UID:10000287-1775070000-1775079000@bluellamaclub.com
SUMMARY:Big Tent ft. Wayne Gerard
DESCRIPTION:Wed | Apr 1	\n\n	Sets 7pm & 8:30pm | $25 Cover \n			\n							RESERVE TABLE\n					\n		https://bluellamaclub.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/WG_SHAPE_SOLO.mp4	\n\n			About the Artist	\n	Grammy-nominated guitarist Wayne Gerard leads Big Tent\, a groove-driven band rooted in funky\, danceable jazz and open improvisation. Joined by Dale Grisa\, John Barron\, Bobby Streng\, and Chaim Tolwin\, the group performs music by Herbie Hancock\, John Scofield\, and The Meters\, alongside Grateful Dead selections reimagined through a jazz lens. Their performances emphasize feel\, interaction\, and real-time musical direction\, with no two shows unfolding the same way. \nHis playing reflects a blues-informed\, groove-centered approach to jazz\, shaped as much by feel and phrasing as by traditional jazz vocabulary. \nHe has collaborated with Kem\, Patti Smith\, Wayne Kramer\, Bob James\, Lenny White\, and Geri Allen\, and is currently touring with Don Was and the Pan-Detroit Ensemble. With Big Tent\, he brings that same depth of experience into a live setting focused on groove\, risk-taking\, and connection between players and audience. \n\n				\n	\n			\n							RESERVE TABLE
URL:https://bluellamaclub.com/event/big-tent-ft-wayne-gerard/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://bluellamaclub.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Wayne-Gerard-1.png
END:VEVENT
